  "body": "**Supplier-boundary audit: an independent, byte-bound check. No new \u03ba, and the selected record is unchanged.**\n\nAll 36 residual wrappers stored in the selected frontier1094 gauge44 word are exact. They satisfy `L \u2218 F_w \u2218 R \u2218 T_E = T_end` on all 512 columns, including global phase. Two independent kernels check this.\n\n- Track: adversarial audit, seed 62.\n- Card: `supplier-boundary-audit`, scope **refined**.\n- Base: `179089e4`.\n- Package: `research/frontier1094-residual-wrappers-seed62/`.\n\n## Why this is needed\n\nLemma A's exact part (`e8-lemma-a-lean`, `e8-lemma-g-lean/PROOF.md` \u00a74) needs a stored wrapper (L, R) for every helper that enters at a nonzero frame E or ends at a hyperplane U. Each wrapper must satisfy `L \u2218 (C_[w] \u2297 I) \u2218 R = T_end \u2218 T_E\u207b\u00b9`. For the selected word these are the 36 records in `RESIDUAL-ADAPTERS.json` (`383f40aa`).\n\nTracing the acceptance in the selected chain:\n- **The bytes are pinned.** Both the owner audit and the certificate's fresh invoice (`input_sha256.fresh_invoice` \u2192 `PREFIX-AND-INVOICE.json` \u2192 `providers.gauge44.artifacts`) pin `RESIDUAL-ADAPTERS.json`. The fresh invoice also pins `WRAPPER-CHECKS.json`.\n- **The chain's own audit checks structure only.** `gauge44-slots-t16/code/audit_allcold.py` (lines 56\u201361) checks only the wrappers' structural fields: frame, terminal, vectors and ranks.\n- **Exactness is established only by the producer's own code.** `hpe_adapters_local.py` generates the wrappers and decodes them again with the same `clifford_exact` primitives, writing `WRAPPER-CHECKS.json` (`PASS_RESIDUAL_WRAPPERS_ARE_EXACT`).\n  - The cold replay re-runs that producer (e.g. `gauge44-slots/construction/slots/verify_slots.py:103`).\n  - No chain code reads the receipt's status or content.\n- **Our merged #1781** checked the child and endpoint records but explicitly left these 36 open.\n\n## Result\n\n`PASS_FRONTIER1094_RESIDUAL_WRAPPERS_EXACT`:\n\n| | Records | Kernel B | Kernel A |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| FULL-ended | 22 | exact | exact |\n| Cold hyperplane-end `0:U` | 12 | exact | exact |\n| Entering hyperplane-end (`2:999`, `3:998`) | 2 | exact | exact |\n\nEvery identity holds on all 512 columns, with the global phase included.\n\n## How\n\n- **Binding.**\n  - The merged #1781 binding is imported with its digests pinned: selected record \u2192 frontier1094 certificate \u2192 capsule \u2192 owner audit \u2192 word and programs.\n  - `RESIDUAL-ADAPTERS.json` must equal the owner audit's own digest.\n  - The `split-centres` decoy has the same basename and is rejected by digest.\n  - The certificate's fresh invoice pins both files' bytes.\n  - The global8 twin is byte-identical.\n- **Inventory.**\n  - The 36 keys are exactly the word's entering helpers ending at FULL (key = start) and its hyperplane-ending helpers (key = start:final).\n  - Every record's frames, vectors and ranks match the word, and all 72 monomials are well formed.\n  - In both programs, each of the 240 wrapped helpers has exactly one `pre` and one `post` residual event, with the correct key. The `pre` comes first and the `post` last.\n- **Kernel B** (`closed_form.py`, new, standard library only) works from closed-form amplitudes: the frame operator's closed formula, the closed form of the monomial records, and F_w as a product of \u221aX gates. It uses sparse exact columns and evaluates no gate lists. Before judging any record:\n  - its frame operator must reproduce #702's 14 frame-kernel digests and #1415's three operator digests;\n  - its monomials and F_w must equal kernel A's on every column.\n- **Kernel A** is #1781's packed evaluator. Both kernels must pass every record; RESULT records 36/36 for each.\n- **Lean pairs.** `3:998` and `2:999` are field-for-field Exact.lean's pair 2 and pair 3.\n\n## Controls\n\nEach mutation is rejected on every record it applies to:\n\n| Mutation | Rejected |\n|---|---|\n| Global phase +1 | 36/36 |\n| Input character (`linear_Z4 += 2`) | 36/36 |\n| CZ term in Q | 36/36 |\n| Offset translation | 36/36 |\n| Swapped wrappers | 36/36 |\n| Width \u22121 and width +1 | 36/36 each |\n| Transposed matrix | 36/36 |\n| Hyperplane-end record against FULL | 14/14 |\n| FULL-ended wrapper reused for a hyperplane end | 2/2 |\n| Another basis of the same span (reordered rows pass) | 2/2 |\n| Kernel B phase and width mutants | 8/8 |\n\nThe tests also reject:\n- the decoy;\n- a mismatched invoice;\n- a flipped archive byte;\n- a dropped `pre` event;\n- a wrong event key;\n- a wrong record vector.\n\nIn the inventory, residual events must be `pre` or `post` only, and every record must have exactly its expected fields.\n\n## Checks run\n\n- `verify.py` passes (about 40 s), and RESULT.json is reproduced byte for byte.\n- All 17 tests pass.\n- `research_package.py --check-only` passes.\n- The registered python3.12 replay gives `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE` (48 s).\n- These were run on Python 3.12.15 and 3.14.8 (macOS 26.5, arm64).\n\n## Overlap\n\n- **The Lean pairs.** `2:999` and `3:998` are the Exact.lean pairs (#593, with #1415's binding). #1611 had tied `2:999` to pair 3 for this word.\n- **The cold rank-4 records.** The eight records `0:124`\u2026`0:327` are byte-identical to records in earlier provider files (e.g. `complex-sw4-frame8-validation`). #702 checked that family's cold wrappers by amplitudes, for PR626.\n- **The four cold hyperplane-end records `0:1000`\u2026`0:1003`.** They are hyperplane cases of #1697's audit of all 511 cold hyperplane terminals, which used wrappers generated by its own run.\n- **What was producer-only.** The 22 FULL-ended entrance wrappers had only producer evidence.\n- **What is new.** All 36 are now checked from the **selected** word's bound bytes, by two kernels, and tied to its programs.\n- Open #1964 (ours, from another session) is about Lemma G H1 extended labels and wrapper placement; that is a different obligation.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR does not show:\n- the executor bridge (Lemma G's H1, and rec(A,B) = record circuit);\n- the identity adapters;\n- Lean proofs beyond the two Exact.lean pairs;\n- any new \u03ba.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/frontier1094-residual-wrappers-seed62/verify.py        # about 40 s\npython3 -I -B -m unittest discover -s research/frontier1094-residual-wrappers-seed62 -p test_package.py\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/frontier1094-residual-wrappers-seed62\n```\n\n## Credit\n\n- **Lean packages:** Lemma A (#516) and Lemma G (#509), both by DreamingOfClouds and formalizing #484.\n- **The wrapper producer:** `hpe_adapters_local.py` (DreamingOfClouds, after PR #458 by chafreaky), using `clifford_exact.py` (icekylinx), which adapts PR425 (jacklightChen).\n- **Exact.lean:** jeremykothe2 (#593).\n- **Calibration sources:** #1415 (commdata2338) and #702 (BigCactusLabs).\n- **Related checks:** #1697 (navinor) and #1611 (bbMisk).\n- **The packed kernel and binding:** our #1781.\n\n## Disclosure\n\nPrepared by Sagar Thakrar (thakrarsagar) with substantial AI assistance from Claude (Anthropic) via Claude Code. Parallel read-only scout and judge subagents selected the obligation; both judges ranked it first. The closed-form kernel, the verifier and the controls were then written fresh. A post-PR adversarial review corrected the supplier trace (the fresh invoice pins the receipt's bytes), the overlap and the credits, and added the kernel cross-check and further controls; these are in the second commit. No claim was posted to Discussions. New material is Apache-2.0.\n",
